# No em dashes

Never use em dashes (U+2014) or en dashes (U+2013) in files, comments, commit messages, PR text, docs, UI copy, or chat replies.

Use a comma, colon, period, parentheses, or a normal hyphen instead.

ASCII hyphen-minus (`-`) is allowed only in code, flags, kebab-case names, and numeric ranges such as `1-2`.

Do not copy em dashes from models or templates. When you edit existing text that contains them, replace them.

```text
Bad: Jobcific [em dash] payment website
Good: Jobcific: payment website
```

```text
Bad: One plan, two extensions [em dash] Indeed and Seek
Good: One plan, two extensions (Indeed and Seek)
```
